PHASE_04=DATABASE_SCHEMA_LIFECYCLE_UPGRADE|Apply additive versioned idempotent Mission Control lifecycle schema migration and migration ledger
PHASE_05=LEGACY_MISSION_COMPATIBILITY|Repair historical mission process reads so pre-schema records return HTTP 200 with explicit NOT_RECORDED_AT_SOURCE_STAGE gaps
PHASE_06=MISSION_LIFECYCLE_CONTROL|Integrate refresh, audit, restart, start-component, add-component, redesign, rollback, pause, resume, validate and stop contracts
PHASE_07=ROLLBACK_AND_RECOVERY_ARCHITECTURE|Bind exact rollback identities, non-restorable semantics, recovery plans and post-effect readback
PHASE_08=MISSION_CONTROL_UI_UPGRADE|Deploy Mission Control UI lifecycle, schema-generation, lineage, gap, component, audit and rollback views
PHASE_09=LPCL_PANEL_RECOVERY_AND_INTEGRATION|Restore 127.0.0.1:8780, integrate LPCL intake with Mission Control lifecycle and prove parser-normalizer compatibility
PHASE_10=HYBRID_COGNITIVE_PLANE_RECONCILIATION|Reconcile local gpt-oss proposal-only plane, external-session SaaS supervisor semantics and no-false-SaaS-answer rule
PHASE_11=MATERIAL_FLEET_REBIND|Rebind or materialize exactly 64 healthy material workers across 12 logical roles without creating a competing Epoch 3 mission
PHASE_12=HOST_AND_WORKTREE_DISCOVERY|Discover all LION worktrees on LION-AUTH-LAB, LAB-UBUNTU, LAB-DEBIAN, MOON and MOON Windows mounts and classify each clean, dirty, ahead, behind or diverged
PHASE_13=LOCAL_REPOSITORY_RECONCILIATION|Preserve operator work, fast-forward clean behind worktrees, retain dirty or divergent work and create explicit reconciliation receipts
PHASE_14=FEDERATION_REACQUIRE_AND_UPGRADE|Reacquire all ten federation repositories, apply only required semantic/documentation deltas, and synchronize without force or no-op commits
PHASE_15=AI_PLATFORM_CANDIDATE_INTEGRATION|Revalidate local candidate d3bf041, archive this LPCL, reconcile source provenance and construct the exact publication candidate
PHASE_16=FULL_LOCAL_VALIDATION|Run full unit tests, Bandit, symbol census, effect inventory, taxonomy, workflow homeostasis, database migration, rollback and UI canaries
PHASE_17=PR337_FAST_FORWARD_UPDATE|Fast-forward the existing PR337 branch to the exact validated candidate and update PR metadata without rewriting history
PHASE_18=EXACT_HEAD_GITHUB_CI|Run and verify all required GitHub CI on the exact new PR337 head and fail closed on any red, missing or stale check
PHASE_19=LIVE_MISSION_CONTROL_DEPLOYMENT|Deploy the validated Mission Control database-lifecycle build with exact service/config/source identity and post-restart readback
PHASE_20=LIVE_LPCL_PANEL_DEPLOYMENT|Deploy or restore the validated LPCL Control Panel on 8780 and verify Mission Control, parser, local model and MAT read-plane integration
PHASE_21=OPEN_MISSION_COMPLETION|Audit and complete, supersede or explicitly retain all prior Epoch 3 missions with lineage and terminal evidence
PHASE_22=ROLLBACK_DRILL_AND_FALSIFICATION|Execute bounded rollback and failure falsifiers without destructive history rewrite and verify recovery semantics
PHASE_23=MERGE_PR337|Merge PR337 only if exact-head CI, local validation, runtime deployment and currentness gates are all green
PHASE_24=POST_MERGE_GLOBAL_SYNC|Reacquire merged master and synchronize every reachable clean ai_platform clone and required federation state while preserving dirty or divergent work
PHASE_25=REMOTE_BRANCH_CLOSURE|Close obsolete mission refs only after merge ancestry, ownership, no-open-PR and readback proofs
PHASE_26=DOCUMENTATION_HOMEOSTASIS|Update multi-level architecture documentation, Mission Control database lifecycle, source provenance, history and AS-IS versus TARGET boundaries
PHASE_27=SIC_TARGET_AND_EPOCH4_SCAFFOLD|Retain Semantic Inference Compiler as candidate-only target and materialize the Epoch 4 scaffolding, contracts and evolution frontier
PHASE_28=RAG_HANDOFF|Produce exact post-merge post-deploy RAG handoff inputs without building the successor RAG
PHASE_29=EPOCH3_TERMINAL_CARRIER|Materialize carrier-last truth binding for repository, GitHub, hosts, databases, Mission Control, LPCL panel, missions and validation
